 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing the county of Madison\nto impose a tax on real estate transfers",
    "basePrintNo": "S7532",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7532-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add Art 31-H §§1449-aaaaaa - 1449-pppppp, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7532\n\nSPONSOR: MAY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing the county of\nMadison to impose a tax on real estate transfers\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nAuthorizes the county of Madison to impose a tax on real estate trans-\nfers of an additional tax on real estate transfers of two dollars\n($2.00) per each five hundred dollars ($500.00).\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: The tax law is amended by adding a new article 31-H, which\nthe county of Madison acting through its local legislative body, an\nadditional tax on real estate transfers of two dollars ($2.00) per each\nfive hundred dollars ($500.00)\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Madison County Board of Supervisors has approved a resolution (No.\n20-281) requesting that the state legislature introduce and enact a bill\nto authorize the country to impose an additional real estate transfer\ntax.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPACT:\n\nNone to state\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2021: A8334 (Salka) Ref to Ways and Means\n2019/2020: A10916 (Salka)\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately and sunsetting after 7 years.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
